# api/ holds exactly one file — the catch-all router — so there is nothing here to exclude.
#
# It used to hold a per-endpoint file as well, and each would otherwise deploy as its own serverless
# function (Vercel's Hobby plan caps a deployment at 12). Every one had to be listed here, and
# api/ai-credits.ts was the one that got missed: it shipped as its own function, never passed
# through jsonRoute, and answered the model account's balance to anyone who asked.
#
# That list is gone because the files are — they were four-line re-exports of handlers the catch-all
# already serves. The rule is now simply that anything in api/ deploys, and
# server/__tests__/apiManifest.test.ts fails the build if a second file appears there.

# A standalone terminal agent kept alongside the app. Nothing imports it and it is never built,
# but without this line it was uploaded on every deploy.
openrouter-agent

# Never bundle local secrets into a deploy — env vars are configured in the Vercel project.
.env
.env.*
